// lexdb over TDS: computed columns (design/lexdb-dialect-gaps.md, package C), checked against SQL Server 2022
// (generated by tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py from mssql_computed_queries.txt): name AS expr [PERSISTED [NOT NULL]]
// at CREATE TABLE and ALTER TABLE ADD, INSERT / UPDATE / MERGE / OUTPUT computing them (271 for a value
// given, 213 for a list that counts them), the expressions refused (1759, 4936, 1046, 207, 8183), NULLs, indexes
// and keys on them, sys.columns, sys.computed_columns and COLUMNPROPERTY, and ALTER COLUMN, DROP COLUMN and
// sp_rename of a column read or computed (5074, 4928, 15336). A column that is not persisted is computed when it is
// read: GETDATE, SYSDATETIME and NEWID in one (a new value at each read, 2729 for an index or UNIQUE on one), an
// error (8134) at the read, not the INSERT, ADD of one over rows. Each expect line: a batch's result sets and counts,
// or its error number. (The last batches, the nd tables, were answered from SQL Server's documentation, by hand:
// no SQL Server was at hand when the virtual columns became read-time ones; regenerating checks them.)
